-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cansaran</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Isolation of DNA for sequence analysis from herbarium material of some lichen specimens.</article-title><source>Turkish J Bot</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>449</fpage><lpage>453</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Ribeiro1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ribeiro</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lovato</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Comparative analysis of different DNA extraction protocols in fresh and herbarium specimens of the genus <italic>Dalbergia</italic>.</article-title><source>Genetic Mol Res</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>187</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Jankowiak1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jankowiak</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Buczkowska</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Szweykowska-Kulinska</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Successful extraction of DNA from 100-year-old herbarium specimens of the liverwort <italic>Bazzania trilobata</italic>.</article-title><source>Taxon</source><volume>54</volume><fpage>335</fpage><lpage>336</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Walters1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walters</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Reilley</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeves</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Baszczak</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>The utility of aged seeds in DNA banks.</article-title><source>Seed Sci Res</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>178</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-May1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ristaino</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Identity of the mt DNA haplotype(s) of <italic>Phytophthora infestans</italic> in historical specimens from Irish Potato Famine.</article-title><source>Mycological Res</source><volume>108</volume><fpage>471</fpage><lpage>479</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Pbo2"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>P&#x000e4;&#x000e4;bo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Molecular cloning of ancient Egyptian mummy DNA.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>314</volume><fpage>644</fpage><lpage>645</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3990798</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Krause1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krause</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dear</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollack</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Slatkin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Spriggs</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Multiplex amplification of the mammoth mitochondrial genome and the evolution of Elephantidae.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>439</volume><fpage>724</fpage><lpage>727</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16362058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003584-Ovchinnikov1"><label>18</